1
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,120
Just try stepping back, won't you?

2
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,260
Those with no money, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,960
I've got none either, but don't you worry.

4
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:36,300
white clouds.

6
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:42,720
Oh well, it'll all work out somehow, right?

7
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:59,900
Those with no jobs, come to my place.

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,520
I've got none either, but don't you worry.

9
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:11,700
Even the crimson clouds are blazing.

10
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

11
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? I get it, I get it.

12
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,460
Got it? Then shut up and follow me.

13
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:43,240
Fly! Magic carpet!

14
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:53,160
Did you make Senior
Terai go on patrol again?

15
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:57,860
Just because Airgunda
is busy making a gas gun,

16
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:01,360
Ryo-chan, you're so naughty!
I'm going to tell the Chief!

17
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,380
That's right.

18
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:06,160
Let's have Chief Ohara drop a
thunderbolt on him once in a while.

19
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,440
Yeah, yeah,
enough to blow the police box sky-high.

20
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,780
Boom, one shot!

21
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:22,260
Senpai...

22
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:22,680
Ryo-chan...

23
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,340
It's not my fault, right?

24
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:29,260
Senpai, where are you?

25
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,720
Ryo-chan, if you're alive, answer me.

26
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,819
Whoa! Oh no!

27
00:02:37,869 --> 00:02:40,660
Ryo-san's been blown to pieces!

28
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:42,460
Aaah!

29
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:46,560
P-pieces! That's just the hand of a traffic safety doll,
you idiot!

30
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,680
So it is.

31
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,840
I'm over here!

32
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:55,440
You're alright, senpai?

33
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,060
What on earth happened?

34
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:01,160
Well, I bought a new airsoft gun
and was just messing around with it.

35
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,860
But this thing guzzles gas,

36
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:09,280
and it burned through all of it in no time.

37
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:13,400
So I figured I'd just
use propane gas instead.

38
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:17,560
I thought this would
definitely boost its power.

39
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:21,220
Apparently the motor's battery shorted out,

40
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:25,060
and it ignited and blew up big time.

41
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:28,740
Well, if you do that,
of course it'd explode.

42
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:31,420
Unbelievable. You brought this on yourself.

43
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:34,540
If the Chief finds out,
you're in big trouble.

44
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:37,700
There's no way we can cover this one up.

45
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:40,560
At times like this,
running away is the best option.

46
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:42,300
See ya!

47
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,520
This is Ryotsu's doing.

48
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:50,040
I'm sorry, Chief. I didn't mean any harm.
I won't do it again.

49
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:53,680
Nakagawa, Reiko, Terai,
you two apologize too.

50
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,300
But that person...

51
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:56,940
It's not Chief Ohara.

52
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:02,180
He's still up to his
usual outrageous antics.

53
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,580
That old wizard.

54
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:05,880
It's been a long time.

55
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:08,840
Oh my, Reiko,
you're still as beautiful as ever.

56
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:10,700
I wasted my time bowing my head for nothing.

57
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:12,900
Can't you see we're busy here?

58
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:15,280
If you have no business here,
get out right now, you damn old geezer.

59
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:19,140
People who make such spiteful
remarks are nothing but trouble.

60
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:19,720
Gar-fire!

61
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,260
Bui!

62
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:25,600
Oink!

63
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,120
Oink oink oink oink oink oink oink oink!

64
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:29,780
Oink oink!

65
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:32,300
If you want me to change you back, repent!

66
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,060
Oink!

67
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:34,920
Oink!

68
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:36,340
Good.

69
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:37,800
Honjara Ga-Fai!

70
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:42,580
Ugh, I've been through hell.

71
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,415
With that magic,

72
00:04:43,465 --> 00:04:46,860
can't you put the police
box back the way it was?

73
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:49,100
Of course, that's easy.

74
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:49,920
Jan-ga!

75
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:51,600
Gigu!

76
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,580
There.

77
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:55,260
Ryo-chan broke it, so ask me properly.

78
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:56,640
I know.

79
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,760
Please, with your magic,

80
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:03,380
could you restore the
police box to how it was?

81
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:07,960
I heard you were going on about
some damn old geezer earlier.

82
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:08,640
Mee!

83
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:11,280
Who on earth said such a thing?

84
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,840
Wasn't it you?

85
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,980
What a thing to say!

86
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:16,180
It was you, Ryo-san, who said it.

87
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,560
Who else could it be but Ryo-chan?

88
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:25,160
I'm sorry! I was so flustered I lost myself!

89
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:28,020
Please, I beg you, do me this one favor!

90
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:31,760
As usual Well, fine!

91
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:32,900
Honjarakai!

92
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:37,860
He's back!

93
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:41,320
What the hell did you come here for, you goddamn old bastard!
Once you're done, get the hell out!

94
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:43,880
Senpai...

95
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:44,260
What?!

96
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:48,300
It's awfully small, though.

97
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:55,820
Could you possibly restore
it to its original size?

98
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,660
Didn't someone just say something
about that goddamn old geezer?

99
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:01,120
You're the one who started it again!

100
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,300
So Ryo-san was the one who said it, right?

101
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:06,100
Don't make us go through this again,
Ryo-chan.

102
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:10,940
Sorry, I lost myself again.

103
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,620
We'd like to ask you too, please.

104
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:16,160
Because we can't get
any work done like this.

105
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:19,300
We just can't refuse a request from Reiko.

106
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,840
Well then, here goes.

107
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:28,060
I'm back, for real this time.

108
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:30,040
What the hell are you doing here,
you damn old geezer?

109
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,800
Once your business is done, get out of here.

110
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,040
Hey, senpai,

111
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:33,760
What?

112
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:38,900
Whoa, you made it bigger this time,
didn't you?

113
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,480
No, it wasn't me, senpai.

114
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,680
Senpai has gotten smaller, you know.

115
00:06:44,260 --> 00:07:04,480
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

116
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,400
Everything's back to normal.

117
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,480
Of course.

118
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,940
This way, we won't get scolded by the Chief.

119
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:10,620
Yeah, that's right.

120
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,280
What a terrible ordeal that was.

121
00:07:14,340 --> 00:07:16,860
By the way, what on earth
did you come here for, old man?

122
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:21,260
I was test-riding a magic carpet I just got.

123
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:23,080
A magic carpet?

124
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:26,000
This one.

125
00:07:36,780 --> 00:07:37,440
Up!

126
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,400
Fly!

127
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:50,920
A flying magic carpet, is it?

128
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,900
Straight out of the Arabian Nights.

129
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:55,200
But the pattern is purely Japanese,
you know.

130
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,380
It suits my taste.

131
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,120
Let me ride it a little too.

132
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Whoa-ho-ho, it's soft!

133
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,940
You'll dirty the carpet. Get off now.

134
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:05,580
Ugh!

135
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,620
Don't drop me like that!

136
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,380
How about it, Reiko? Why don't you ride too?

137
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:12,460
Really?

138
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,480
If you're a beauty, you're most welcome.

139
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:18,720
I'm holding on tight.

140
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,300
Fly!

141
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:30,060
How wonderful.

142
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,460
It looks so refreshing, doesn't it?

143
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,360
There's no traffic jams
up in the sky, either.

144
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,820
Wait a minute.

145
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:40,980
If we use that well,
we could make a fortune.

146
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:44,660
Well, I suppose it's about time I head home.

147
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,640
Thank you so much for everything.

148
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,320
No need to thank me.

149
00:08:50,100 --> 00:08:51,300
Where's Ryo-san?

150
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,240
Hold on, please.

151
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,000
What is it?

152
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,800
Please, let us at least repay you.

153
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,100
Repay me, you say?

154
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:59,820
He's up to something again, isn't he?

155
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:01,720
What are you talking about?

156
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,840
He changed me back to normal.

157
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:06,520
Thanking him is only natural
for a human being, right?

158
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:09,880
Reiko, you even got to
ride his magic carpet!

159
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:11,600
You love it that much?

160
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,880
W-well, that's...

161
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:14,520
Please, this way.

162
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:20,040
I'm afraid we couldn't
prepare anything grand, though.

163
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:22,760
This is the legendary fine sake!

164
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,500
Isn't this Kameari's famous nabe!

165
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,260
Come, come, your glass!

166
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:27,800
And some snacks, too.

167
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:30,780
Senpai, drinking alcohol on duty?

168
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,560
It's not like I'm the one drinking it.

169
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,920
He can really hold his liquor.

170
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,640
Come on, one more cup!

171
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:47,200
Don't hold back, keep drinking!

172
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,380
If he keeps drinking at this pace,

173
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:54,720
Sure, sir, you're a good drinker,
so one more cup!

174
00:09:54,720 --> 00:10:04,060
So he finally passed out after all.

175
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:07,300
For a guy who loves sake,
he's a real lightweight.

176
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:09,620
He's fallen asleep. What should we do?

177
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:14,220
He is our benefactor,
so let's have him rest here.

178
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,720
Well then, the futon -

179
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:19,000
I'll take care of it,
so you lot get back to work.

180
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,380
You're going to drink the leftover sake,
aren't you?

181
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:22,400
We wouldn't do that.

182
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:26,040
It's this one I have business with.

183
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:34,620
Magic carpet, go!

184
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:39,540
First it has to float, right?

185
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:42,340
- What's that sound?
- Are you all right?

186
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,060
Uh-oh. Brace yourselves.

187
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:48,520
Fly! Full speed!

188
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:58,820
Too fast! Stop! Stop!

189
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:18,260


190
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:34,220
Damn, that was a terrible experience.

191
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:46,720
But once you get used to it,
it's actually pretty comfortable.

192
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,260
Shall we get started?

193
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:53,220
Come one, come all,
if you're not in a hurry,

194
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:54,920
step right up and take a look!

195
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:57,480
A magic carpet,
the rarest thing in the world!

196
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:59,520
If you think it's a lie, just watch!

197
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,940
Chimpui-pui carpet, come and see!

198
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:03,840
Wow!

199
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:06,480
What on earth is going on?

200
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:07,720
Is it some kind of magic trick?

201
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,100
Isn't it rigged up on wires?

202
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:11,620
No tricks, no gimmicks here.

203
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:13,700
It's a genuine magic carpet!

204
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:14,920
Well, what do you say?

205
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:18,580
Take a sightseeing flight
over Tokyo on a magic carpet!

206
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:23,120
And right now, to celebrate our opening, it's
half price at just ten thousand yen per hour!

207
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:26,000
How about it, young man?

208
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,040
A date on the world's first flying
carpet will be a memorable one.

209
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,240
The world's first

210
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:35,980
A date in the sky sounds lovely!
Let's go for a ride.

211
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:37,440
Yeah, let's.

212
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:39,380
Thank you very much for your business!

213
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:41,980
Okay, hop on, hop on!

214
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,680
Excuse me.

215
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:47,840
Alright, we're taking off!

216
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:51,300
Chichin puipui! Carpet, fly!

217
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:55,500
Whoa!

218
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:56,180
Whoa!

219
00:12:56,180 --> 00:13:04,420
Whoa!

220
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:04,660
Whoa!

221
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:10,160
Whoa!

222
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:12,020
Whoa!

223
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:12,060
Whoa!

224
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:12,180
Whoa!

225
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:12,260
Whoa!

226
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:12,340
Whoa!

227
00:13:12,340 --> 00:13:12,880
Whoa!

228
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:12,900
Whoa!

229
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,160
Whoa!

230
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:14,900
Whoa!

231
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:17,980
Don't lean out so far, or I'll get angry.

232
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:21,460
Why, it's Honda!

233
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:25,400
Sir, we're going to take a little detour.

234
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:28,360
Whoa!

235
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:34,000
Whoa!

236
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,240
Gah!

237
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,300
Yo, Honda.

238
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:43,720
Good sir,
I'm afraid we're rather busy at the moment.

239
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,760
If you've got business, come back later.

240
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:49,380
Don't be so stiff,
just take a look over here.

241
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:51,320
No matter what, you absolutely have to -

242
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:53,800
What's that, then?

243
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,760
It's a magic carpet, how about that?

244
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:59,700
A magic carpet, I never knew something
like that existed in this world!

245
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:27,460
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

246
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:30,960
Boss, we're in trouble! A police
motorcycle is chasing us through the sky!

247
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:35,560
Don't be ridiculous!
Motorcycles don't fly through the sky!

248
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,600
It's true! Just look!

249
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:40,800
Stop daydreaming in broad daylight!

250
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:43,420
Idiot!

251
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:47,240
Look closely!
That's not a police motorcycle flying!

252
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:49,820
It's just a flying carpet with
a police motorcycle sitting on it!

253
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,320
You're right!

254
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:52,520
Whoa!

255
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:55,400
Start dash!

256
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:56,540
Yaah!

257
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:30,780
Are we gonna let our prey get away?

258
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,460
Looks like we lost the White Plum

259
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:45,380
Atabo, you think I'd get
caught by the White Plum?

260
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:46,860
Yeah, right?

261
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:51,220
Stop the car and come quietly.

262
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:54,300
Does anyone stop just
because they're told to?

263
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:02,660
Damn it! Fall already!

264
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:03,160
Idiot!

265
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:08,660
Stop them! Bullets!

266
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,360
Right, take the shot!

267
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:20,740
Those fools.

268
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:34,200
Damn, how did we let
that big money slip away?

269
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,120
I'm going to the toilet for a sec.
Keep an eye on the carpet.

270
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,080
Leave it to me.

271
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:48,920
Have a good trip.

272
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:52,920
Oh my, this part's a little frayed.

273
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:57,980
I wonder if they sell sewing kits.

274
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:04,600
There's a carpet just lying around here.

275
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:08,100
Someone might mistake it for trash,
so let's take it with us.

276
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:09,260
Yeah.

277
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:12,560
That feels better.

278
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:13,940
Right, let's go.

279
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,880
Where'd the carpet and Honda go?

280
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:24,460
Senpai.

281
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:28,540
Honda, where'd the magic carpet go?

282
00:17:28,660 --> 00:17:30,000
It's not here? Did it turn red?

283
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:33,240
It's gone.

284
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,160
What?

285
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:36,200
I told you to keep an eye on it.

286
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,760
Search! Find it!

287
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:39,840
Could be.

288
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,040
Y-yes!

289
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:43,020
Ikkirin!

290
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:43,940
Mm. Mm.

291
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,740
Mm. Aaaaaaah!

292
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:59,080
Senpai, I found a really ominous sign...
"The 5th Chūtanku!"

293
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,640
About ten times.

294
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:04,500
Eeeeeeeh!

295
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:09,960
But the two who bumped into the thing...

296
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,000
Yes.

297
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,740
The magic carpet...

298
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:16,920
There it is!

299
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:18,500
Yes.

300
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:21,420
What are you doing?

301
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,880
Senpai, are you okay?

302
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,500
A rainbow?! It's burnt to a crisp!

303
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,480
It still has its shape, at least.

304
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,320
Crash!

305
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,320
Oh no, the magic carpet...

306
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:55,420
Senpai, don't lose heart.

307
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,486
Easier said than done,

308
00:18:57,536 --> 00:19:00,260
even if we tell it to fly now,
it's not going to fly, is it?

309
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:05,880
Stop! Come back!

310
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,100
Wait, what's going on?

311
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:10,958
Could it be...

312
00:19:11,008 --> 00:19:14,680
maybe the magic power remains even as ash.

313
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:18,800
Scoop up this ash! Carefully!

314
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:19,940
Ash?!

315
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:27,780
I've come to make one
final request to you all.

316
00:19:27,780 --> 00:19:31,100
I'm Tobe Tobe Tobe Yuichi.

317
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:38,420
In tomorrow's election, please support Tobe Tobe
Tobe Yuichi as your citizens' representative.

318
00:19:46,140 --> 00:19:47,820
The carpet's flying this way!

319
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:51,980
Come back!

320
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:55,220
Come back!

321
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:56,640
Come back!

322
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,180
Come back!

323
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:58,620
Come back!

324
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:00,080
Get back here!

325
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,120
Come back!

326
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:05,400
Come back!

327
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:05,420
Come back!

328
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:06,600
Come back!

329
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:07,300
Come back!

330
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:08,060
Come back!

331
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:17,700
Come back!

332
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:21,340
They say if we return it right away,
they'll forgive us.

333
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:24,020
Give it back quietly, Ryo-chan.

334
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:29,020
Why the refusal?

335
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:31,180
What are we going to do, senpai?

336
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:34,000
The magic carpet's completely burned up,
you know.

337
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,600
In a situation like this,
of course they'll run away, obviously.

338
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:41,840
What are you doing?

339
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:44,280
If we do it right,
we should be able to fly with this.

340
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,980
Let's put the rest in our pockets.

341
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:52,140
Hold on tight, Mr. Ryotsu.

342
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:53,980
Alright, not "make it fly," but fly!

343
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:58,460
Hey, wait up!

344
00:20:58,860 --> 00:20:59,660
Can you wait?

345
00:21:02,820 --> 00:21:03,540
Look.

346
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:05,940
Wait!

347
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:07,140
Here we go!

348
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:13,880
I've been wondering about
something for a while now.

349
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:16,380
What is it, Kei-chan?

350
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,880
The carpet the senior officer
took was the magic carpet, right?

351
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,880
Why is a police motorcycle
flying through the sky?

352
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:25,260
Now that you mention it, that's right.

353
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:27,880
Could they be hiding it somewhere?

354
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:29,420
No, that couldn't be it.

355
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:33,100
And we can't explain the
motorcycle flying, either.

356
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:37,620
Could that guy have taken
my precious magic carpet?

357
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:41,260
What are you doing?

358
00:21:41,260 --> 00:21:42,660
Shoot it down, will you?

359
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:44,360
Hide it!

360
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,400
Aaaaaah!

361
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:47,180
Aaaaaah!

362
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:55,300
Aaaaaah!
Have you forgotten that I have magic powers?

363
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:57,220
Aaaaaah!

364
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:00,240
Aaaaaaah!

365
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:00,680
Aaaaaaah!

366
00:22:02,580 --> 00:22:02,980
Me!

367
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:26,820
Tobe! In tomorrow's election, Tobe!

368
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,520
Please support Tobe!

369
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:31,340
Tobe! Tobe! It's Tobe!

370
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:34,760
Tobe! Tobe! Please support Tobe!

371
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:40,780
Aaaaaaah!

372
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:43,220
Tobe! Yuichi is really flying!

373
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:45,560
Tobe! Tobe! Tobe is flying!

374
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,640
It's coming!

375
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,680
Yes! This time, left!

376
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:18,840
Senpai...

377
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:21,640
Ryo-chan,
what on earth is going to happen to us?

378
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:25,420
Give up! I'll strangle you in heaven!

379
00:23:31,700 --> 00:23:32,920
It finally stopped.

380
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:34,120
Senior Swiss

381
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:40,860
You are completely surrounded.

382
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:43,520
Trespassing into heaven is a serious crime.

383
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,360
Submit to subjugation quietly.

384
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:48,860
By the way,
a hellish interrogation awaits you.

385
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:51,060
Becoming the hands of evil.

386
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,680
To think we'd end up tasting hell!

387
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:56,160
What the hell is going on here!

388
00:23:56,880 --> 00:24:00,680
Damn it! I hate these goddamn magic carpets!

389
00:24:01,180 --> 00:24:02,360
Yeah!

390
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:03,700
Yeah!

391
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:18,760
Na na na na, na na na na, na na na na

392
00:24:19,860 --> 00:24:24,280
for those who gamble foolishly on looks,

393
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:27,460
I probably don't want to become that.

394
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:32,060
if you're dawdling at the street corner,

395
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:34,620
Take Star

396
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:38,000
because now isn't everything.

397
00:24:38,900 --> 00:24:42,640
don't get too worked up about it.

398
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:46,360
even if you tell a few
lies or cheat a little,

399
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:50,520
sometimes you're helping someone.

400
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:52,520
Baby, do you know me?

401
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:56,960
Facing tomorrow with a nice spirit!

402
00:24:58,020 --> 00:25:01,960
Don't rot away, just do what needs doing.

403
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:11,540
If it's hard to understand,
it's because I want it to look that way.

404
00:25:11,540 --> 00:25:17,300
Isn't it better than a makeover?

405
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:24,780
Na na na na na na na na na na na na

406
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:47,700
Nice to meet you!

